WEBVTT

00:01.415 --> 00:13.306
[SPEAKER_01]: At 2 p.m. on the 4th of Wealsun, Paul Rivero exits the Warrens with his prisoners returning to the Alchemy building.

00:15.147 --> 00:27.599
[SPEAKER_01]: So you walk into the thing and your guys walk by and the sergeant that was with you says, here, these are prisoners for the Royal Dungeons.

00:28.697 --> 00:31.058
[SPEAKER_01]: I assume you can take these, captain.

00:31.258 --> 00:33.098
[SPEAKER_01]: And he says that to Rodiger.

00:33.438 --> 00:33.798
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

00:34.138 --> 00:38.119
[SPEAKER_01]: Rodiger says, men, they go and grab them.

00:39.140 --> 00:46.301
[SPEAKER_01]: And he comes up to you and says, Sir, we found the body of an old man.

00:46.441 --> 00:47.442
[SPEAKER_01]: The fire's been put out.

00:47.502 --> 00:52.403
[SPEAKER_01]: We found the body of an old man and the sewer's below the building.

00:55.782 --> 00:56.882
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, thank you.

00:56.942 --> 00:59.543
[SPEAKER_00]: Take them back to the Royal Dungeon.

00:59.583 --> 01:00.903
[SPEAKER_00]: Show me where the body is, please.

01:01.463 --> 01:02.643
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, come this way.

01:04.144 --> 01:16.926
[SPEAKER_01]: You walk into the building, the smell of fire still there, and actually the stench of the chemicals in the area, pretty acrid to the nose.

01:17.266 --> 01:23.368
[SPEAKER_01]: However, the place is not as damaged as you would have thought it was, right?

01:23.788 --> 01:24.028
[SPEAKER_00]: Mm-hmm.

01:25.029 --> 01:25.449
[SPEAKER_01]: Interesting.

01:25.810 --> 01:37.680
[SPEAKER_01]: You walk down this spiral staircase into the sewers where there's this running river that goes from the harbor district and then it turns towards the seawall.

01:38.220 --> 01:41.623
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, this is the way the sewage in the city is moved off.

01:41.903 --> 01:42.384
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

01:42.684 --> 01:51.632
[SPEAKER_01]: And there on the stone walkway at the bottom of the stairs, you see the old man.

01:53.865 --> 02:02.510
[SPEAKER_01]: Laying there with a stab wound in his eye and some weird black acre coming out of the wound.

02:05.491 --> 02:06.692
[SPEAKER_01]: A black like ooze?

02:07.112 --> 02:07.452
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

02:08.153 --> 02:09.654
[SPEAKER_01]: Like some kind of poison.

02:10.294 --> 02:11.735
[SPEAKER_00]: The skin is discolorized.

02:11.875 --> 02:14.836
[SPEAKER_00]: I want to take a vial if I can and get that.

02:15.257 --> 02:20.760
[SPEAKER_01]: Alright, so you tell Rodiger, fetch me, you know there are vials upstairs.

02:20.840 --> 02:21.200
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

02:21.340 --> 02:22.961
[SPEAKER_01]: Fetch me a vial from upstairs.

02:24.583 --> 02:25.684
[SPEAKER_01]: And what do you do?

02:25.764 --> 02:26.184
[SPEAKER_01]: You look?

02:27.846 --> 02:31.309
[SPEAKER_00]: I kind of bend down and I just look, yeah.

02:31.429 --> 02:31.689
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

02:33.070 --> 02:33.450
[SPEAKER_00]: So yeah.

02:33.510 --> 02:35.172
[SPEAKER_00]: And this is the old alchemist?

02:35.332 --> 02:36.333
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the alchemist.

02:36.793 --> 02:38.334
[SPEAKER_01]: He's obviously been killed.

02:38.534 --> 02:38.775
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

02:39.635 --> 02:39.895
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

02:42.638 --> 02:47.121
[SPEAKER_01]: Anyway, Rodiger comes down with the vial.

02:48.983 --> 02:51.785
[SPEAKER_01]: And I assume you take it.

02:52.305 --> 02:52.526
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

02:53.472 --> 02:56.014
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you take your dagger and scoop something in?

02:56.034 --> 02:56.234
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

02:57.094 --> 02:58.275
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a weird liquid.

02:59.255 --> 02:59.736
[SPEAKER_01]: Black.

03:01.077 --> 03:03.658
[SPEAKER_01]: But it almost flows like mercury.

03:04.519 --> 03:05.019
[SPEAKER_01]: Weird.

03:05.459 --> 03:07.821
[SPEAKER_01]: Into the test tube.

03:07.901 --> 03:09.702
[SPEAKER_01]: And you get a little dropper of it.

03:10.943 --> 03:11.323
[SPEAKER_01]: Right?

03:12.263 --> 03:19.047
[SPEAKER_01]: And you sit there looking at it in the torch light that Rodiger holds above you.

03:19.708 --> 03:22.470
[SPEAKER_01]: Very strange little BB of blackness.

03:23.533 --> 03:25.354
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically quicksilver, but dark.

03:25.974 --> 03:27.594
[SPEAKER_01]: However, there is a shimmer to it.

03:27.675 --> 03:28.615
[SPEAKER_01]: Very strange.

03:29.515 --> 03:29.895
[SPEAKER_01]: Weird.

03:32.556 --> 03:32.936
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

03:33.417 --> 03:33.877
[SPEAKER_00]: Interesting.

03:36.518 --> 03:38.438
[SPEAKER_01]: Rodiger says to you, do you know what that is?

03:38.478 --> 03:40.719
[SPEAKER_00]: No, I don't.

03:44.200 --> 03:45.021
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll find out, though.

03:48.322 --> 03:48.842
[SPEAKER_01]: You take it.

03:50.523 --> 03:51.103
[SPEAKER_01]: Cap it off.

03:52.318 --> 03:53.301
[SPEAKER_01]: And put it in your pouch.

03:58.130 --> 04:03.813
[SPEAKER_00]: Is there anything else on the walls, on the drawers, or anything like that that's so important?

04:04.294 --> 04:05.795
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you don't see anything in the sewer.

04:06.055 --> 04:08.416
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, we're in the sewer?

04:08.576 --> 04:09.937
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you had to go down into the sewer.

04:09.957 --> 04:11.158
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the guy's body was.

04:11.898 --> 04:14.200
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you want to have it taken out, or what do you want to do?

04:14.500 --> 04:16.041
[SPEAKER_00]: No, I'll just hold onto that myself.

04:16.741 --> 04:18.742
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you want his body taken out?

04:19.303 --> 04:20.743
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, have his body taken out.

04:21.944 --> 04:23.245
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you want to give orders to...

04:26.020 --> 04:26.420
[SPEAKER_00]: Rodiger?

04:27.100 --> 04:27.540
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, sure.

04:28.360 --> 04:30.281
[SPEAKER_00]: Rodiger, take this body out.

04:33.981 --> 04:35.202
[SPEAKER_00]: Where should I have it taken?

04:35.222 --> 04:42.623
[SPEAKER_00]: I want it to be analyzed.

04:45.483 --> 04:46.704
[SPEAKER_01]: Take it back to the royal palace?

04:46.984 --> 04:47.664
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, please.

04:48.924 --> 04:50.164
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, under my name.

04:51.424 --> 04:52.065
[SPEAKER_01]: We have the cards.

04:53.305 --> 04:54.065
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, thank you.

04:59.042 --> 05:01.744
[SPEAKER_00]: So I was told that Jude went down these sewers.

05:02.304 --> 05:04.926
[SPEAKER_00]: Is there any means that I can tell which way they went?

05:07.508 --> 05:08.869
[SPEAKER_01]: Did they come back the way they came?

05:11.631 --> 05:12.031
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

05:13.112 --> 05:18.576
[SPEAKER_00]: The only way out is through the pipes, and he points to the rivulet that goes towards the sea.

05:19.496 --> 05:21.918
[SPEAKER_01]: It's possible they fell in the water and went downstream.

05:23.983 --> 05:29.385
[SPEAKER_01]: Where they ended up, I don't know, there are grates on all of the pipes that go through the sewers.

05:29.786 --> 05:33.167
[SPEAKER_01]: There are other places they may have been able to come out, manholes and such.

05:34.968 --> 05:35.188
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

05:36.268 --> 05:36.708
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

05:39.830 --> 05:42.491
[SPEAKER_00]: Um...

05:45.912 --> 05:47.293
[SPEAKER_00]: If I were a Jew, what would I do?

05:47.313 --> 05:49.294
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know.

05:49.654 --> 05:51.415
[SPEAKER_00]: I'd probably kill someone, but...

05:52.687 --> 05:53.227
[SPEAKER_01]: If he could.

05:53.768 --> 05:54.288
[SPEAKER_00]: If he could.

05:55.288 --> 05:56.669
[SPEAKER_00]: And he's with some other boy.

06:02.631 --> 06:04.972
[SPEAKER_00]: Hmm.

06:05.012 --> 06:07.593
[SPEAKER_00]: Alright, I think the best move is to just go back to my palace.

06:08.334 --> 06:08.634
[SPEAKER_00]: Alright.

06:09.234 --> 06:20.239
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you go with Rodiger and the rest of the troops, with the prisoners, and walk up the row of gods.

06:22.816 --> 06:31.500
[SPEAKER_01]: Towards the palace, trying your best to act like one of the guardsmen instead of trying to be Paul Rivero.

06:33.280 --> 06:35.441
[SPEAKER_00]: Why do I try to act to be a guard member?

06:35.781 --> 06:41.784
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't want to, if you want people to know that Paul Rivero is down there with a mask, that's fine.

06:42.084 --> 06:42.604
[SPEAKER_01]: That's cool.

06:44.325 --> 06:44.945
[SPEAKER_00]: Nah, it's okay.

06:44.965 --> 06:46.486
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll just go back and...

06:47.855 --> 06:49.197
[SPEAKER_00]: To be honest, I don't really care.

06:49.337 --> 06:50.618
[SPEAKER_00]: It's at nighttime anyways.

06:50.979 --> 06:51.119
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

06:51.279 --> 06:52.861
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there are people on the street watching.

06:57.366 --> 06:57.786
[SPEAKER_01]: So what?

06:58.087 --> 06:58.707
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

07:00.550 --> 07:00.990
Okay.

07:01.310 --> 07:03.533
[SPEAKER_01]: So you walk back to the Royal Palace.

